+[Fast Feedforward 3D Gaussian Splatting Compression](19199-fast-feedforward-3d-gaussian-splatting-compression.md) is an autoencoder-based compression method that encodes 3D Gaussian attributes into a latent space using hyperpriors and context models, addressing the fidelity drop caused by the non-invertibility of MLPs in geometry attributes. Unlike anchor-based quantization methods that modify Gaussian locations and require finetuning, FCGS creates context grids in a feed-forward manner without altering the original Gaussian positions.
 
-### Deformation Field MLP
-#### definition
-- [S3] An MLP network $F_\theta$ that maps 3D Gaussian coordinates and time to deviations in position, rotation, and scaling.
-#### step
-- [S3] Input: 3D Gaussian coordinate $x$ and time $t$. Process: Pass through eight fully connected layers with ReLU activations and 256-dimensional hidden layers to output a 256-dimensional feature vector. Concatenate the feature vector and the input in the fourth layer. Output: Pass the feature vector through three additional fully connected layers (without activation) to separately output offsets $\delta x, \delta r, \delta s$ for position, rotation, and scaling.
-#### parameter
-- [S3] Hidden layer dimension: 256.
-- [S3] Number of initial fully connected layers: 8.
-- [S3] Number of output layers: 3 (one for each offset).
-- [S3] Activation function: ReLU for hidden layers, none for output layers.
-- [S3] Additional storage compared to 3D Gaussians: 2MB.
-#### comparison
-- [S3] Does not use grid/plane-based structures because dynamic scenes have higher rank than static scenes, and explicit point-based rendering exacerbates this rank.
+### [SHARE](19401-share.md)
+[SHARE](19401-share.md) is a pose-free framework for generalizable 3D Gaussian splatting that estimates camera poses via predicted rays and uses anchor-aligned coarse-to-fine geometry estimation to predict 3D Gaussian parameters without ground-truth poses. It sets itself apart from sibling methods like [PixelSplat](16423-pixelsplat.md) and [MVSplat](16423-mvsplat.md) by explicitly embedding pose awareness into multi-view cost volumes via Plücker rays, making it robust to pose inaccuracies where generalizable 3D Gaussian splatting methods are highly sensitive.
 
-### RnD-Avatar
-#### definition
-- [S4] A 3DGS-based human avatar modeling framework that reconstructs animatable and relightable human avatars from monocular video by decomposing geometry and appearance attributes and using dynamic skinning weights for pose-variant deformation.
-#### step
-- [S4] Encode Gaussian attributes using the Gaussian Attributes Encoder $D_G$, which consists of two sub-encoders $D_g$ and $D_a$. Both are multi-layer perceptrons (MLPs) that take the Gaussian position $x$ as input and output the corresponding geometric and appearance attributes, respectively.
-- [S4] Articulate the human avatar by applying Linear Blend Skinning (LBS) transformations using the dynamic skinning weights $W_{\Theta_t}$ to deform the 3D Gaussians from canonical space to posed space.
-- [S4] Optimize the RnD-Avatar through a Physically-Based Rendering (PBR) process to optimize geometric attributes (position and normal) and appearance attributes (albedo, roughness, and visibility).
-- [S4] Render photorealistic images given an environmental light by performing a PBR process on the optimized avatar.
+### [Feed-Forward Hierarchical Gaussian Diffusion](19615-feed-forward-hierarchical-gaussian-diffusion.md)
+[Feed-Forward Hierarchical Gaussian Diffusion](19615-feed-forward-hierarchical-gaussian-diffusion.md) is a feed-forward reconstruction method for computed tomography (CT) that predicts a set of 3D Gaussian primitives from degraded projections without per-scene optimization. It solves the problem of sparse-view, low-dose, or limited-angle CT reconstruction by using two explicit Gaussian banks (structure and detail) initialized from anatomical cues and refined via a sequential structure-to-detail diffusion hierarchy. It differs from single-bank Gaussian reconstruction by maintaining separate banks for global attenuation geometry and residual detail, and from dense voxel diffusion by operating on explicit Gaussian primitives with a sequential hierarchy.
 
